  "contract": [
    "PublishCatalog validates an ordinary permitted catalog before reading the durable predecessor.",
    "A first publication uses sequence one. Later publications advance the stored sequence without wrapping.",
    "The complete source input and stored sequence identify exact retries after reopen or an ambiguous successful response.",
    "Changed proposals require the exact predecessor. Competing writers cannot both publish different successors.",
    "BootstrapCatalog explicitly adopts an ordinary store and cannot reset an established authority.",
    "Unknown permission semantics, changed identity, failed reads, exhausted sequence, and stale proposals cause refusal.",
    "A successful publication still requires serving-client activation. No automatic stale-proposal retry occurs."
